# Vampire Gourmand: whenever it attacks, Bot1 may sacrifice another creature; if Bot1 does, it draws a card and the Gourmand can't
# be blocked this turn (CR 701.21a, 608.2c, 509.1b). Bot1 sacrifices its Memnite. The Gourmand itself, Bot2's Ornithopter and
# Bot1's Mox Jets (not creatures) are not choices ("another" excludes the source; a player sacrifices only what they control),
# and Memnite and Ornithopter can't both go: the sacrifice is of one. Bot2's Ornithopter would have blocked, but can't.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Jet
Vampire Gourmand
Memnite
Ornithopter
Island
Island
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Vampire Gourmand.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Vampire Gourmand)
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Choose(Vampire Gourmand)
! Bot1.Choose(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
! Bot1.Choose(Mox Jet)
! Bot1.Choose(Memnite; Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Choose(Memnite)
! Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Vampire Gourmand)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = false
Bot1.Hand.Count = 3
Bot2.Life = 18
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = false
